From 425b28ec0ebc454eb22c630f3258d5a22c416eee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 08:34:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] fp8 : fix activation encoder saturation + M3/M4
 completion

- fp8.cuh: fp8_e4m3_from_f32 saturated all E>=15 values (the 256-448
  top range of each 128-block) to 448, inflating activations; fix
  saturates only for E>=16 or the E=15/man3=7 NaN pattern. This was
  the root cause of PPL 23.8 vs 9.89 bf16 (2.4x), ~2.0 logit shifts,
  and generation divergence at token 10. After the fix: PPL 9.99
  (< 1% of bf16), 20-token greedy parity exact.
- fp8.cu: batched mul_mat (loop over ne12*ne13) so llama-server's
  4-sequence batches work; supports_op drops the b->ne[2]*ne[3]==1
  restriction.
- --vocab-file override: llama_model_params.vocab_file +
  common_params_model.vocab_file + arg.cpp (env LLAMA_ARG_VOCAB_FILE).
- llama-safetensors: edge-case hardening (E5M2/unknown dtype rejection,
  non-128 fp8 k-dim rejection, corrupt-header wrap, missing scale_inv).
- M3: mmproj verified end-to-end (llama-cli + llama-server + image API);
  llama-server loads the fp8 dir + mmproj.
- M4: PPL, greedy parity, 3-GPU row-split parity, memory footprint
  (14.3GB vs 17.8GB bf16 on 1 GPU at full 262144 context).

